From 057e501f92c02c320cf1989006d856959e20f630 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ponytail <ponytail@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:42:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] lite: numeric Shortcut video quality with honest fallback

/api/lite/video accepts q=360/480/720/1080 (missing q defaults 480;
an invalid explicit q is a JSON 400 before any resolve). The
normalizer dedupes per distinct quality tier first, then pins one
representative per requested tier (1080/720/480/360) BEFORE the
16-tier global cap, so no pile of unrelated heights can starve the
requested tiers or the 360 fallback; it keeps only finished H.264
video-only formats with a finite short side inside 144..1080, best
first. The planner picks the exact requested tier or the highest
below it, never upscales, and the muxed fallback binds real
dimensions/codecs from the resolver: best candidate at or below the
request, actual height reported, upward or unsupported pairings
rejected with a JSON 502. info=1 reports requested, chosen and
available tiers plus the actual fallback height when engaged.

The range downloader shares safeGet's full trust boundary via
core/net-safe.js: addresses are parsed to their normalized 128-bit
form (expanded, compressed and mapped notations of the same address
classify identically) and embedded IPv4 is classified as IPv4. IPv6
fails closed: only global unicast (2000::/3) is reachable, minus the
IANA special-purpose registry (2001::/23 protocol assignments except
the explicit globals, 2001:db8::/32 and 3fff::/20 documentation,
2002::/16 6to4) - site-local, discard-only, benchmark, tunneling,
link-local, ULA, multicast and unallocated space are all rejected
for every pinned hop; lite.js uses the same module. One abort-driven wall
deadline spans dns, redirects, headers and body - a trickling body
can no longer outlive it. Redirect, probe and refused bodies are
drained under a hard cap, responses destroyed on refusal paths, the
probe must answer exactly the requested 0-0 interval, at most five
validated redirects, strict 206 Content-Range match on interval and
total per chunk, streaming per-chunk and cumulative byte caps before
any write, zero-progress chunks retried then failed, and it returns
bytes actually written rather than the claimed total.

The lite cache key is versioned (lite2-<q>) so a pre-fix file under
the old id+q key is invalidated, never served, and pulled audio and
muxed output are ffprobe-verified against the selected plan before
serving: h264 video, aac audio, and the actual short side
(min(width,height), portrait included) at or under the planned tier -
unknown dimensions are refused, and a copy-muxed non-aac "m4a" can
no longer pass. The limits test hook exists only under
RJ_TEST_HOOKS=1. Native fixtures drive real range downloads and a
real ffmpeg remux, plus lying-upstream cases: oversized chunk,
start/total mismatch, zero-byte 206, redirect loop, lying probe
interval, trickle body past the wall deadline, non-aac audio,
portrait short-side, stale cache key, and post-remux cap rejection.
